  "query_preview": "..\n\nA fast, progressive flow will persist over the northern CONUS over \nthe next week, although a deeper trough does look to develop over \nNew England on Monday. \n\nRain looks to be coming to end by around 8 AM, with the 850 MB theta-\ne ridge already well southeast of the state. A shortwave trough is \nworking through the northern Great Lakes this morning, with an \nimpressive mid level dry slot arriving, as 700 MB dew pt depressions \nreach 30 to 50 C by day's end. \n\nExpansive high pressure builds in tonight, with the center of the \nhigh (1028 MB) parked over northern Lower Michigan by 12z Saturday. \nNBM temps on are on the colder side. With this morning's rainfall \nsoaking the ground and a lack of strong dry advection near the \nsurface, surface dew pts are expected to remain solidly above \nfreezing; thus, no frost is expected. In fact, there is more concern \nwith northerly flow off Lake Huron leading to low clouds over the \neastern Thumb region, keeping overnight mins elevated above 40 \ndegrees. \n\nSlow return flow around the departing high on Saturday, but backed \nsoutheast surface flow should keep temps in the low to mid 60s, \nslightly below normal. \n\nThe next Pacific shortwave currently along the southern British \nColumbia coast on track to move into the central Great Lake Saturday \nnight, with the cold front moving through on Sunday. The greatest \nheight falls and forcing will be directed toward Saginaw Bay. Euro \nensembles suggests significantly higher pops for the northern half \nof the CWA than the dry outgoing NBM pops. Nonetheless, GFS does \nshow the moisture axis (850-700 MB theta-e ridge) getting strung out \nand weakening/drying up as it moves through Lower Michigan. \n\nOutside of the low chance pops late Saturday night into Sunday \nmorning, dry weather will be the rule early next week as upper level \nconfluent flow supports another round of good subsidence and strong \nhigh pressure building over Lower Michigan. This high brings a \nbetter chance for temps to fall into the 30s for Tuesday morning. \nHowever, Euro ensemble members are mainly indicating mins aoa 40 \ndegrees.",
